WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.680
Heart. Plus 'gone'.
心，加上“消失”。

00:03.680 --> 00:07.360
Put them side by side: 忙 — busy.
把它们左右放在一起：忙——busy。

00:07.360 --> 00:11.040
Stack them: 忘 — to forget.
把它们上下叠起来：忘——to forget。

00:11.040 --> 00:14.720
Same two pieces.
还是同样两个部件。

00:14.720 --> 00:18.400
The only difference is the floor plan.
唯一的区别是布局。

00:18.400 --> 00:22.080
In Chinese, layout carries meaning.
在中文里，布局也承载意义。

00:22.080 --> 00:25.760
Where you put a piece changes what the word is.
你把部件放在哪里，会改变这个字是什么。

00:25.760 --> 00:29.440
It's LEGO, but the instructions matter.
它像乐高，但说明书很重要。

00:29.440 --> 00:33.123
There's a game where you do exactly this — build characters from pieces, and the arrangement is part of the puzzle.
有一款游戏正是这样玩——用部件搭出汉字，而排列方式本身就是谜题的一部分。
